# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# ── Signing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Prefer a Foundry keystore over a raw private key. `PRIVATE_KEY` in a dotfile is one
# `cat` away from a screen share, one misdirected paste away from a chat window, and it
# sits in your shell history the moment you `export` it:
#
#   cast wallet import botchain-deployer --interactive
#   forge script ... --account botchain-deployer
#
# The key is then encrypted at rest and prompts for a password at use. Only fall back to
# PRIVATE_KEY if the keystore genuinely will not work for your setup.
#
# PRIVATE_KEY=0x...

# ── Endpoints ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BOTCHAIN_RPC_URL=https://rpc.botchain.ai
BOTCHAIN_TESTNET_RPC_URL=https://rpc.bohr.life

# ── Deploy parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Address that receives the initial supply and any admin role. Set it deliberately —
# a deploy that mints to the wrong address is not undoable.
# TREASURY=0x...
